WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.444 --> 00:00:16.530
"Gum?" said in surprise.

2
00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:19.151
"Are you sure that's all that's in there?"

3
00:00:20.051 --> 00:00:21.612
"Yeah," said Maggie.

4
00:00:21.632 --> 00:00:23.633
"Is our next clue in there?"

5
00:00:23.653 --> 00:00:25.674
"Um let's see."

6
00:00:26.414 --> 00:00:28.695
Luke turned the container upside down and shook it.

7
00:00:29.535 --> 00:00:31.056
Some tissue paper fluttered out.

8
00:00:31.436 --> 00:00:33.137
Then a folded piece of paper fell out.

9
00:00:34.017 --> 00:00:35.578
Maggie picked up the folded paper.

10
00:00:35.598 --> 00:00:37.199
"It's another clue.

11
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.921
So this is definitely the right box," she said.

12
00:00:40.941 --> 00:00:45.504
"Hey, William, why would your parents give us a few lousy sticks of gum?

13
00:00:46.684 --> 00:00:47.985
That's not much of a treasure."

14
00:00:48.005 --> 00:00:50.326
"Shh," Henry shushed her.

15
00:00:50.987 --> 00:00:52.067
Maggie was being rude.

16
00:00:52.948 --> 00:00:55.109
"It is kind of weird," Cole said.

17
00:00:55.129 --> 00:00:57.250
"Do pirates even chew gum?"

18
00:00:58.411 --> 00:00:59.211
Nathan shrugged.

19
00:00:59.231 --> 00:01:01.592
"I don't think so," he said.

20
00:01:01.612 --> 00:01:04.334
"I doubt they can get it on the high seas."

21
00:01:05.395 --> 00:01:06.115
Luke laughed.

22
00:01:06.836 --> 00:01:08.797
"Maybe they steal it from the ships they raid."

23
00:01:09.658 --> 00:01:12.500
He tilted his pirate hat and then pretended to swing his sword.

24
00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:14.621
"Ahoy, mateys!

25
00:01:15.262 --> 00:01:17.943
Give me your gum, or I'll make you walk the plank!"

26
00:01:18.904 --> 00:01:21.606
Nathan pretended to fight back with an invisible sword.

27
00:01:21.626 --> 00:01:23.267
"No way!"

28
00:01:23.727 --> 00:01:24.228
he cried.

29
00:01:24.248 --> 00:01:27.630
"I'll die before I hand over my gum!"

30
00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:31.285
"Stop messing around, you guys," Maggie said.

31
00:01:31.305 --> 00:01:35.427
"Seriously, why would William's parents give us gum?

32
00:01:36.188 --> 00:01:38.329
It doesn't fit in with the pirate theme at all."

33
00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.832
Henry didn't say anything, but he had to agree.

34
00:01:41.852 --> 00:01:43.213
"Oh well."

35
00:01:45.995 --> 00:01:47.516
Cole grabbed one of the sticks of gum.

36
00:01:47.536 --> 00:01:50.918
"At least we can chew gum while we follow the next clue."

37
00:01:51.819 --> 00:01:54.000
Then he looked at the gum and wrinkled his nose.

38
00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.182
"Yuck," he added.

39
00:01:56.202 --> 00:01:57.823
"Never mind.

40
00:01:58.523 --> 00:01:59.464
It's watermelon.

41
00:02:00.168 --> 00:02:01.109
I hate that flavor."

42
00:02:01.129 --> 00:02:03.390
"Watermelon? Cool!"

43
00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.531
Luke grabbed another stick of gum.

44
00:02:06.452 --> 00:02:07.412
"That's my favorite.

45
00:02:08.213 --> 00:02:11.074
I buy this gum at the general store every time I come here.

46
00:02:12.035 --> 00:02:14.857
Anna's store is the only place I know that sells this brand."

47
00:02:15.737 --> 00:02:17.758
"Your family owns a general store?"

48
00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:19.239
Maggie asked Anna.

49
00:02:19.259 --> 00:02:24.702
"Great deduction, detective Maggie," Nathan said sarcastically.

50
00:02:25.743 --> 00:02:27.664
Henry was surprised by Nathan's remark.

51
00:02:28.604 --> 00:02:32.706
"Is Nathan still mad at Maggie for grabbing the map away from him earlier?"

52
00:02:33.046 --> 00:02:33.686
Henry thought.

53
00:02:34.446 --> 00:02:35.747
That wasn't like Nathan at all.

54
00:02:36.287 --> 00:02:37.588
He almost never got mad.

55
00:02:38.208 --> 00:02:40.709
And even if he did, he didn't stay mad for long.

56
00:02:40.729 --> 00:02:46.011
"My family's store is one of the oldest businesses in Sea Cove," Anna told Maggie.

57
00:02:46.031 --> 00:02:50.033
"My great-grandfather started the store a long time ago.

58
00:02:50.833 --> 00:02:52.374
Everyone in town shops there."

59
00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:54.555
Luke grinned and blew a bubble.

60
00:02:54.575 --> 00:02:59.549
"Yeah. They have the best gum in town!"

61
00:03:00.369 --> 00:03:02.490
Cole tossed his gum back into the container.

62
00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:08.234
"I still think a few sticks of gum is a weird prize," he said.

63
00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.835
"Especially for a pirate treasure hunt.

64
00:03:11.455 --> 00:03:13.256
Are you sure we found the right box, William?"

65
00:03:13.276 --> 00:03:15.117
"How should I know?"

66
00:03:15.538 --> 00:03:16.858
William snapped with a frown.

67
00:03:16.878 --> 00:03:20.781
"I didn't have anything to do with this stupid scavenger hunt."

68
00:03:21.721 --> 00:03:22.802
Cole looked surprised.

69
00:03:22.822 --> 00:03:24.823
"Okay," he said.

70
00:03:25.823 --> 00:03:26.764
Henry bit his lip.

71
00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.361
Everyone seemed a little grouchy right now.

72
00:03:29.381 --> 00:03:32.322
"Why don't we go see if lunch is ready?"

73
00:03:32.682 --> 00:03:33.402
he suggested.

74
00:03:33.422 --> 00:03:36.844
"Maybe we can ask William's parents about the gum."

75
00:03:36.864 --> 00:03:39.325
"Good idea," Cole agreed.

76
00:03:39.345 --> 00:03:41.966
"All this treasure hunting has made me hungry."

77
00:03:48.088 --> 00:03:49.269
They headed back to the house.

78
00:03:49.989 --> 00:03:52.590
A lunch of sandwiches and juice was set out on the deck.

79
00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:57.072
William's parents were there too, sipping tall glasses of iced tea.

80
00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:02.081
As the kids sat down to eat, they told William's parents about how the treasure hunt was going

81
00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:02.561
so far.

82
00:04:03.482 --> 00:04:06.823
When they got to the part about the gum, William's mother looked surprised.

83
00:04:06.843 --> 00:04:09.203
"Gum?" she said.

84
00:04:09.223 --> 00:04:11.444
"I didn't put any gum in the box."

85
00:04:12.444 --> 00:04:13.104
Maggie nodded.

86
00:04:13.124 --> 00:04:15.525
"The next clue was in the box too."

87
00:04:16.445 --> 00:04:18.986
She took the piece of paper out of her shorts pocket and held it up.

88
00:04:19.846 --> 00:04:21.907
William's parents traded a confused look.

89
00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:24.988
"Are you sure there wasn't a white envelope in the box too?"

90
00:04:25.288 --> 00:04:26.408
William's father asked.

91
00:04:27.476 --> 00:04:29.178
"We're sure," Henry said.

92
00:04:29.198 --> 00:04:34.963
"There was nothing inside except the clue, some tissue paper, and a few sticks of gum."

93
00:04:34.983 --> 00:04:36.905
"What was in the envelope?"

94
00:04:37.245 --> 00:04:38.646
Luke asked William's parents.

95
00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:41.569
"Your booty," William's father answered.

96
00:04:41.589 --> 00:04:44.392
"Seven movie tickets—one for each of you."

97
00:04:44.412 --> 00:04:46.373
"Movie tickets?"

98
00:04:46.814 --> 00:04:47.494
Maggie said.

99
00:04:48.415 --> 00:04:49.496
William's mother nodded.

100
00:04:49.516 --> 00:04:53.320
"Not just ordinary movie tickets, either," she said.

101
00:04:54.124 --> 00:04:57.306
"They were for the local premiere of Revenge of the Pirate's Ghost."

102
00:04:58.287 --> 00:04:59.187
The kids gasped.

103
00:04:59.948 --> 00:05:03.310
That was the title of the new pirate movie that was coming out next month.

104
00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.131
"Revenge of the Pirate's Ghost?"

105
00:05:06.511 --> 00:05:07.272
Nathan cried.

106
00:05:07.292 --> 00:05:09.493
"I'm dying to see that!"

107
00:05:09.513 --> 00:05:12.055
"You know what this means, don't you?"

108
00:05:12.415 --> 00:05:13.055
Maggie said.

109
00:05:13.075 --> 00:05:15.257
"What?" Luke asked.

110
00:05:15.277 --> 00:05:18.479
"Someone stole our pirate booty."

111
00:05:19.199 --> 00:05:20.720
Maggie glanced at Henry and Cole.

112
00:05:21.433 --> 00:05:24.263
"This is a job for The Lemonade Detectives!"
